_🇸🇪 Denna sida finns även på_ [_svenska_](/mtbo-oringen) _🇸🇪_

Mountain bike orienteering (MTBO) is an established and popular discipline at O-Ringen, welcoming international elite riders, juniors, masters and newcomers alike. You can either enter a multi-day competition class by age category (W/M10 to W/M85) or ride individual days in an Open class where you choose your own course length and start time. All maps follow the international MTBO specification (ISMTBOM) showing track rideability, and controls are punched contactlessly at speed using SportIdent Air+ (SIAC).

In 2027, O-Ringen comes to Stockholm and the MTBO discipline is staged across three days from Monday 26 July to Wednesday 28 July. Stage 1 (middle distance) takes place on the island of Lidingö in a hilly, trail-dense recreational forest area, while Stage 2 (sprint) and Stage 3 (long distance) share the same arena at Brantbrink in Tullinge, the clubhouse of Tullinge SK. Together, Lidingö's dense singletrack network and the fast Södertörn ridges around Brantbrink offer three distinct days of riding right by the Swedish capital.

